#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""tamias-driver-actions — the interaction-actions demo driver.

A self-contained demo driver (Python 3 stdlib only) that exercises
the `invoke` wire op and the declarative action layer end-to-end:

- `DriverManifest.actions[]` — global verbs covering all three
  `DangerLevel`s (`none`/`confirm`/`type-target`) and every
  `ParamKind` (`string`, `text`, `number`, `integer`, `bool`,
  `enum`, `date`, `ref`, `string[]`).
- `NodeBase.actions[]` — a node-scoped `board.export` action on the
  tasks table.
- `TreeItem.actions[]` — per-row `task.*` actions on every backlog
  tree item.
- `contributes.menus[]` — command-palette entries mixing `action`
  and `route` kinds, with sections, keywords, and priorities.
- `{"op":"invoke",…}` — the dispatch handler; mutations are
  in-memory for the life of the `serve` process and answered with a
  fresh `view` so hosts can re-render (the refresh-after-mutation
  contract).

Wire surface (ndjson JSON-RPC over `serve`, one JSON object per line):

    {"op":"manifest"}                      -> DriverManifest
    {"op":"views"}                         -> [ViewSummary, ...]
    {"op":"view","view":"board"}          -> ViewResult
    {"op":"query","query":"tasks",...}    -> QueryResult
    {"op":"invoke","view":"board",
     "action":"task.new","params":{…}}    -> ActionResult

`tamias-driver-actions manifest` and `tamias-driver-actions
capabilities` answer the discovery probes pavo runs before spawning
`serve`.
"""

